  lessons: [
  {t:"What e-PRO Is, and the Licence Underneath It", d:"Certification vs. license, NAR membership, course structure", len:"12 min",
   script:"The e-PRO certification is awarded by the National Association of REALTORS through its Center for REALTOR Development. Like every credential in this family it is a certification and not a license. Before it can mean anything you must hold an active real estate license from your state real estate commission and maintain membership in the National Association of REALTORS at local, state and national level. The programme is a two-part course. Day one covers the changing market, reputation management and core technology. Day two, delivered online, covers social platforms and advanced tools. Then you pay a one-time application fee. There is no proctored exam and no annual renewal."},
  {t:"Digital Marketing Foundations", d:"The funnel, lead magnets, CRM discipline", len:"20 min",
   script:"Start with the funnel: awareness, interest, decision, action. A digital lead enters at the top with almost no relationship to you, which is exactly how it differs from a referral, and it needs nurturing rather than closing. A lead magnet is what you trade for an email address — a neighbourhood market report, a home valuation, a first-time buyer guide. A customer relationship management system is where every one of those leads lives afterward, with a next action and a date attached. The single biggest failure in agent marketing is not lead generation. It is leads arriving in a system nobody works."},
  {t:"Web Presence, IDX and Local SEO", d:"Agent sites, MLS feeds, Google Business Profile", len:"22 min",
   script:"Your website has to be fast, mobile-first, and carry an I D X feed. I D X stands for Internet Data Exchange, the arrangement that lets you display Multiple Listing Service listings on your own site under your M L S's display rules. Most agent lead flow comes from local search rather than national search, so a complete and active Google Business Profile, a steady flow of reviews, and pages written about actual neighbourhoods will outperform generic content every time. Put the call to action above the fold, where a visitor sees it without scrolling, and make it a single obvious next step."},
  {t:"Social Media and Paid Advertising", d:"Organic reach, paid social, retargeting, video", len:"22 min",
   script:"Organic reach on the major social platforms has been falling for years, so treat organic as brand-building and paid as distribution. Retargeting is the highest-value paid tactic available to an agent: a tracking pixel on your site lets you show ads to people who already visited, which is a far warmer audience than any cold interest targeting. Video is still undervalued in this business. Listing walkthroughs, neighbourhood tours and short vertical clips all outperform static posts. Two cautions: fair housing law applies in full to ad targeting, and every platform's real estate ad category restricts the audience options you are allowed to use."},
  {t:"Email, Automation and Settlement-Era Compliance", d:"Drip campaigns, listing alerts, advertising rules", len:"22 min",
   script:"Email remains the highest return per dollar and per hour for most agents. Build a drip campaign for new leads, automated listing alerts for active buyers, and a database touch for past clients. Track conversions so you can attribute closed business to a channel rather than guessing. Then the compliance half. Since the National Association of REALTORS settlement practice changes took effect in August of twenty twenty-four, your marketing may not state or imply that buyer representation is free. Compensation offers cannot be published on a Multiple Listing Service, and your written buyer agreement must be signed before you tour a home."},
  {t:"Your State Real Estate License", d:"State-specific — updates automatically per state", len:"20 min", stateSpecific:true,
   script:null},
  ],

